<code>assert \old(this.size()) - 1 == this.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.size()) - 1 == this.size();</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.size()) == \result ? \old(this.size()) : \old(this.size()) - 1 == this.size();</code>

However, since the method returns `true` only if a word was removed, we can simplify the assertion to reflect that the size decreases by 1 when a word is removed:

<code>assert \result => \old(this.size()) == this.size() + 1;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.size()) - this.size() == 1;</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \old(this.size()) - 1 == this.size();</code>
--------------------
